PROBE - does the reachability suite still bite after the rename?

Issue koniz-dev/flutter-starter#160 wired test/core/startup/startup_reachability_test.dart
to the exact factory main() calls, so that a regression in the container
fails the suite. The rename moved both sides at once, which could in
principle have left the test driving something other than production.
This probe removes the never-retry policy from the production factory and
shows the suite goes red. The edit is reverted at the end of this log.

$ git diff -- lib/main.dart

diff --git a/lib/main.dart b/lib/main.dart
index 49c8280..3910f4f 100644
--- a/lib/main.dart
+++ b/lib/main.dart
@@ -62,7 +62,7 @@ Duration? _neverRetry(int retryCount, Object error) => null;
 ProviderContainer createAppContainer({
   List<Override> overrides = const <Override>[],
 }) {
-  return ProviderContainer(retry: _neverRetry, overrides: overrides);
+  return ProviderContainer(overrides: overrides);
 }
 
 // Returns a Future so callers can await startup. `void main() async` would

